                <pb facs="0145" n="137" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg137"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94 Conference/154: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-11-01T19:00:00+00:00">November 1, 1937—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 1—3:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>683. Your 433, October 31, 2 p.m. communicated orally and confidentially to the
                    Foreign Secretary. He said that it confirmed his view <pb facs="0146" n="138"
                        xml:id="pg138"/> that statements from this type of Japanese can not be taken
                    as really representing the views or intentions of the Japanese Government.</p>
                <p>Eden leaves tonight for Brussels.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bingham</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
